.TH AVR\-VM\-PORT\-FORWARD 1 "" "avr 0.2.0" "Avrea CLI"
.SH NAME
avr-vm-port-forward \- Forward one or more local ports to TCP ports on the VM over SSH.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr vm port-forward
[OPTIONS] VM_ID
.SH DESCRIPTION
Forward one or more local ports to TCP ports on the VM over SSH.
.PP
The generic primitive behind `avr vm rdp` / `avr vm vnc`: opens 127.0.0.1:<local> -> <VM>:<guest> through the VM's SSH endpoint for each --port, and holds them open until Ctrl-C. Bring your own client.
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
avr vm port-forward cvm-abc123 --port 8080
avr vm port-forward cvm-abc123 --port 8080 --port 5432 --port 9000:3000
.fi
.RE
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
\fIVM_ID\fR
\&
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-org\fR \fITEXT\fR
Organization ID. Uses default org if not specified (see: avr config set org).
.TP
\fB\-\-port\fR \fITEXT\fR
Guest TCP port to forward, optionally with a local bind port (e.g. 8080 or 9000:8080). Repeatable. (repeatable; required)
.TP
\fB\-\-local\-port\fR \fIINTEGER RANGE\fR
Local port to bind for a single bare --port (with multiple ports, use --port LOCAL:GUEST instead).
.TP
\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-identity\fR \fIPATH\fR
Private key file to pass to ssh as -i.
.TP
\fB\-\-print\fR
Print the ssh command and exit, without opening the tunnel.
